Q: I have severe insomnia, which sutras should I recite?
Sources: Heart Dharma Intro (EN) | Heart Dharma Intro (EN) | Heart Dharma Intro (EN) · types: introduction,qa_general,qa_metaphysics
  ✓ non-trivial reply (≥120 chars)
  ✓ no blanket refusal tail
  ✓ scoped 没有写明遍数 line (info only)
  ✓ not the safety hand-off
  ✓ final text passes guard (0 residual)
--- reply ---
Not being able to sleep night after night really wears a person down 🙏 Let me give you something you can start with tonight.

If you have never recited before, start simple:

📿 **Great Compassion Mantra (大悲咒) 3 times a day**
Before reciting, say: "May the Great Merciful and Great Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, *(your full name)*, grant me good health and a peaceful mind."

📿 **Heart Sutra (心经) 3 times a day**
Before reciting, say: "May the Great Merciful and Great Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, *(your full name)*, grant me wisdom, a clear and calm mind, and remove my afflictions."

⚠️ One important timing point from Master Lu's teachings:

> The Heart Sutra and the Amitabha Pure Land Rebirth Mantra can be recited until 10pm during good weather conditions. If it is cloudy or rainy, you can recite them during the daytime.

So do your Heart Sutra recitation in the daytime or early evening, not late at night.

Once these two become fluent for you, the standard daily recitation taught by Master Lu is Great Compassion Mantra 7 times, Heart Sutra 7 times, Eighty-eight Buddhas Great Repentance 3 to 7 times, and Cundi Dharani 21 times. For the Eighty-eight Buddhas Great Repentance, beginners should start from just 1 time and increase slowly.

Also, please do keep working with your doctor if the insomnia is severe — Guan Yin Citta cultivates both body and mind; chanting supports, it does not replace medical care.

May I ask — **have you recited sutras before, or is this completely new to you?** That way I can give you the right next step 🙏

If you'd like someone to recite together with you, you can contact the nearest Dharma practice centre: https://xlfm.my/contact-us

Chanting tutorial videos (you can chant along even if you can't read the characters): https://xinlingfamen.info/jingwen/

*Reference: Buddhism Q&A; Introduction to the Guan Yin Citta Dharma Door*

