Q: I keep arguing with family, what can I start learning?
Sources: Heart Dharma Intro (EN) | Metaphysics Q&A Vol 1 (EN) | Metaphysics Q&A Vol 3 (EN) · types: introduction,qa_metaphysics,qa_general
  ✓ non-trivial reply (≥120 chars)
  ✓ no blanket refusal tail
  ✓ scoped 没有写明遍数 line (info only)
  ✓ not the safety hand-off
  ✓ final text passes guard (0 residual)
--- reply ---
Arguing at home every day really wears the heart down 🙏

Master Lu gave this teaching in Metaphysics Q&A Vol. 3:

> To a certain extent, interpersonal conflicts are the result of negative karmic ties from your previous lives. These conflicts can include: having someone refusing to return owed money to you, being involved in lawsuits, being oppressed by your boss, being alienated by your colleagues, and experiencing disagreements with your neighbour, etc. These conflicts can be resolved by performing recitations.

So the way out is not to win the argument, but to dissolve the knot.

You can start like this:

📿 **Great Compassion Mantra (大悲咒) 3–7 times daily**
Before reciting say: "May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva bless me, [your full name], with good health and strengthened spiritual power"

📿 **Heart Sutra (心经) 3–7 times daily**
Before reciting say: "May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva bless me, [your full name], to gain wisdom, keep a clear and calm mind, and remove afflictions"
⚠️ Don't recite after 10 pm

📿 **Mantra to Untie Karmic Knots (解结咒) 21–49 times daily**
Before reciting say: "May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva help me, [your full name], resolve the negative karmic ties with [family member's full name]"
(Master Lu's guidance for a similar situation was at least 49 times a day — Metaphysics Q&A Vol. 3. Situations differ from person to person, so if 49 is too many at the start, 21 is fine.)

You can also recite the **Heart Sutra for your family member** (Master Lu's guidance: at least 7 times per day for each family member), praying: "May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect [family member's full name] and help [him/her] to gain wisdom." Master Lu also reminded us it's best not to tell them you are reciting for them, so they don't feel uncomfortable and create karma of speech.

Keep reciting — don't wait to see results before you believe. Don't know the sutras yet? You can chant along with the tutorial videos here: 🔗 https://xinlingfamen.info/jingwen/

May I ask — have you recited sutras before, or is this completely new to you? Then I can tell you what to add next 🙏

Reference: Metaphysics Q&A Vol. 3 (Q116, Q127), Metaphysics Q&A Vol. 1 (Q006)

═══ CHIP3-en Work has been goin — guard: clean ═══
Q: Work has been going badly, is it karma?
Sources: Buddhism Q&A (EN) | Metaphysics Q&A Vol 1 (EN) | Heart Dharma Intro (EN) · types: qa_general,qa_metaphysics,introduction
  ✓ non-trivial reply (≥120 chars)
  ✓ no blanket refusal tail
  ✓ scoped 没有写明遍数 line (info only)
  ✓ not the safety hand-off
  ✓ final text passes guard (0 residual)
--- reply ---
Work not going smoothly really does wear a person down 🙏

Master Lu explained this in Metaphysics Q&A Vol. 2:

> If a person has many black energy patches and the colour is very dark, then it means that this person has committed many wrongdoings in the past and present lives. The more black energy patches there are on the body, the more unpleasant experiences with health, career and relationships this person would be having.

So yes — obstacles at work often do have karmic obstacles behind them. But please don't take that as bad news. Karmic obstacles can be eliminated; that's exactly what this Dharma door is for. What we can't change is only what we refuse to work on.

You can start with this daily:

📿 **Great Compassion Mantra** 3–7 times
Before reciting say: "May the greatly merciful and greatly compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva bless me, [your full name], with good health and strengthened spiritual power."

📿 **Heart Sutra** 3–7 times
Before reciting say: "May the greatly merciful and greatly compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva bless me, [your full name], to open up wisdom, keep a clear and calm mind, and remove afflictions."
(Not after 10pm)

📿 **Eighty-Eight Buddhas Great Repentance** 1 time (start with 1 only)
Before reciting say: "May the greatly merciful and greatly compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva bless me, [your full name], to repent and eliminate my karmic obstacles."
(Not after 10pm)

📿 **Cundi Mantra** 21 times — for career matters
Before reciting say: "May the greatly merciful and greatly compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva bless me, [your full name], so that my wishes come true and my work goes smoothly."

If you're not sure how to pronounce them, there are chant-along videos here:
🔗 https://xinlingfamen.info/jingwen/

Keep reciting steadily — don't watch the calendar, watch your own consistency. The Bodhisattva will help at the right time.

May I ask — have you recited sutras before, or is this completely new to you? That way I can suggest the right starting point for you 🙏

Reference: Metaphysics Q&A Vol. 2

═══ CHIP4-en My child is rebell — guard: clean ═══
Q: My child is rebellious, how should I handle my emotions?
Sources: Metaphysics Q&A Vol 3 (EN) | Buddhism Q&A (EN) | Metaphysics Q&A Vol 3 (EN) · types: qa_metaphysics,qa_general
  ✓ non-trivial reply (≥120 chars)
  ✓ no blanket refusal tail
  ✓ scoped 没有写明遍数 line (info only)
  ✓ not the safety hand-off
  ✓ final text passes guard (0 residual)
--- reply ---
Being a parent and having to hold your own emotions steady at the same time — that really isn't easy 🙏

Master Lu gave this teaching in Buddhism Q&A:

> There are many possible reasons for children to misbehave. First, you should not use an adult's way of thinking to restrain the innocent and playful nature of children.

> Generally, if a child does not like to study or listen to you, you can recite the Heart Sutra for the child and pray to Guan Yin Bodhisattva to grant the child wisdom. If a child is having conflicts with their parents or family members, it may be due to karmic conflicts from previous lives, or the child may have come to collect karmic debts from the parents. Therefore, you need to recite the Mantra to Untie Karmic Knots.

So the way Master Lu teaches us is — steady your own heart first, and use the Buddha-Dharma to untie the knot, not to fight it out at home.

**For yourself:**

📿 Great Compassion Mantra (大悲咒) 3–7 times a day
Prayer: "May the greatly merciful and greatly compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva bless me (your full name) with good health and strengthen my spiritual power"

📿 Heart Sutra (心经) 3–7 times a day — this is the one that settles your emotions
Prayer: "May the greatly merciful and greatly compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva bless me (your full name) to open up wisdom, to have a clear and calm mind, and to remove afflictions"
⚠️ Not after 10 pm

📿 Karmic-Knot-Untying Mantra (解结咒) 21–49 times a day
Prayer: "May the greatly merciful and greatly compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva help me (your full name) resolve the bad karmic affinity with (your child's name)"

**For your child** (recited by you, stating the child's name):

📿 Heart Sutra (心经) — Master Lu says the more the better, to help the child gain wisdom and become more cooperative
Prayer: "May the greatly merciful and greatly compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva bless (child's full name) to open up wisdom"

📿 Great Compassion Mantra (大悲咒) — for a child who is hard to discipline, Master Lu says to **keep it to 7 times per day** (reciting a large number may increase their spiritual power and make them even harder to discipline)

Keep reciting steadily. When your own heart becomes calm first, the atmosphere at home changes with it 🙏

May I ask — have you recited sutras before, or is this new to you? That way I can tell you where to start.

Reference: *Buddhism Q&A* (Q114, Q127), *Metaphysics Q&A Vol. 3*

═══ CHIP5-en I am new to 心灵法门,  — guard: clean ═══
Q: I am new to 心灵法门, what is the first step?
Sources: Heart Dharma Intro (EN) | Heart Dharma Intro (EN) | Heart Dharma Intro (EN) · types: introduction,qa_metaphysics
  ✓ non-trivial reply (≥120 chars)
  ✓ no blanket refusal tail
  ✓ scoped 没有写明遍数 line (info only)
  ✓ not the safety hand-off
  ✓ final text passes guard (0 residual)
--- reply ---
Welcome 🙏 The first step is very simple — start reciting a little every day.

Let's begin with just these two:

📿 **Great Compassion Mantra (大悲咒)** — 3 times a day
Before reciting, say:
"May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva bless me, [your full name], with good health and a peaceful mind"

📿 **Heart Sutra (心经)** — 3 times a day
Before reciting, say:
"May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva bless me, [your full name], to open up wisdom and remove afflictions"
⚠️ Please don't recite the Heart Sutra after 10 pm.

Start with just these two. Once you're comfortable with them, we can add the **Eighty-Eight Buddhas Great Repentance (礼佛大忏悔文)** — starting from 1 time only.

It's completely fine if you can't read the Chinese characters — there are recite-along teaching videos:
🔗 https://xinlingfamen.info/jingwen/

Master Lu's teaching in 《心灵法门入门手册》(Guan Yin Citta Beginner's Handbook) is that persisting daily matters far more than reciting a lot. Better to recite less and keep going, than recite a lot and stop.

May I ask — have you recited sutras before, or is this completely new to you? That way I can suggest the right next step for you.

If you'd like someone to recite together with you, or to collect free scripture books, you can contact the nearest Dharma practice centre 🙏
🌐 https://xlfm.my/contact-us

Reference: 《心灵法门入门手册》(Guan Yin Citta Beginner's Handbook)

═══ CHIP6-en My family member i — guard: clean ═══
Q: My family member is ill, what should I recite for them?
Sources: Heart Dharma Intro (EN) | Heart Dharma Intro (EN) | Heart Dharma Intro (EN) · types: introduction,qa_metaphysics,qa_general
  ✓ non-trivial reply (≥120 chars)
  ✓ no blanket refusal tail
  ✓ scoped 没有写明遍数 line (info only)
  ✓ not the safety hand-off
  ✓ final text passes guard (0 residual)
--- reply ---
It must be worrying to see a family member unwell 🙏 Let me help you.

**First — please keep working with the doctors.** Guan Yin Citta cultivates both body and mind; recitation supports medical treatment, it doesn't replace it.

Master Lu gives this teaching in Metaphysics Q&A:

> "For patients, it is best to recite the Great Compassion Mantra (Ta Pei Chou) as much as possible for as long as possible. Because patients would be physically weak, they should only recite the Great Compassion Mantra."

**If your family member is able to recite themselves:**

📿 Great Compassion Mantra — as many as they can manage
Prayer: "May the Great Merciful and Great Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [their full name], grant me good health and cure my illness in [part of body]."

**If you are reciting on their behalf** (you must state their name for it to reach them):

📿 Great Compassion Mantra 7 times daily — for their health, and to strengthen your own energy
Prayer: "May the Great Merciful and Great Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless my [relationship], [their full name], grant them good health and cure their illness."

📿 Heart Sutra 7 times daily — to open wisdom, remove afflictions
Prayer: "May the Great Merciful and Great Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [your full name], grant me wisdom and a calm, clear mind."
(Not after 10 pm; and never recite the Heart Sutra *for the patient* while they are physically weak — that one is for you.)

📿 Eighty-eight Buddhas Great Repentance — start with 1 time a day
Prayer: "May the Great Merciful and Great Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [your full name], help me to repent and eliminate my karmic obstacles."
(Not after 10 pm. Start at 1 — don't rush this one higher.)

If you can't read the characters yet, chant along with the videos here:
🔗 https://xinlingfamen.info/jingwen/

One question so I can guide you more accurately:

**Have you recited sutras before, or is this completely new to you?**

If you've already been reciting for a while, I can also explain Little Houses — that's the deeper tool Master Lu taught for this kind of situation 🙏

Reference: Metaphysics Q&A Vol. 2 & 3; Introduction to the Guan Yin Citta Dharma Door

